                <pb facs="1042" n="914" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg914"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 691.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Baker</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 24,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 60.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 49, of the 23d ultimo, and to approve your revival of the question of the
                    custody of ships’ papers in Venezuelan ports, which it announces. You will press
                    the subject with all due earnestness to a successful conclusion. The
                    Department’s recent instruction respecting the matter will demonstrate its
                    importance.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
